  "General": {
    "Time": "2021-05-17T13:19:29.441Z",
    "Iscps": null,
    "Agency": "CW",
    "Author": "NnekaWhite",
    "Source": "0bdda2ab-b74f-4d74-ba17-3b9b37a9ca19",
    "Purpose": "247a8b26-cdee-4ce8-b36e-b37e49fd0103",
    "Lastname": "Conyers",
    "countyid": "1b7ae41e-e77a-4a1e-a0a3-cda5292cde0b",
    "Firstname": "Sierra",
    "Narrative": "<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Reporter:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sierra Conyers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Baltimore City DSS</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">443-423-7371</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Casehead:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Johnses Johnson (8/20/98)</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">4400 Old Court Road Apt A</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pikesville, MD 21208</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">443-204-0964</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Children:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Major Morris (7/30/17)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sierra Conyers with Baltimore City CPS called to report suspected abuse/ neglect of Major Morris (3 yrs). Caller informed that she received a call from Morgan Johnson (443-304-8292), Major’s aunt at 9:17 am with concerns regarding her sister, Johnses Johnson. Morgan informed that Johnses has a controlling boyfriend named Larry who controls her actions both inside and outside of the home. She also has random men come in the house and smoke weed. Morgan reported that Larry hits Major and Major has been struck in the face, lip, and lower backside by Larry. This happened 3 days ago. Morgan said that at first Major lied and said he fell, then he said that Larry hit him. Morgan has seen the lower back injuries on Larry. Morgan said that she feels that Johnses may be in danger due to the domestic violence disputes. Caller informed that she called 911 and an Officer is going out to the home to assess the safety of Major and his mother. She realized soon after that Ms. Johnson resides in Baltimore County.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">This writer called to speak with Morgan Johnson to get more information regarding her concerns. Ms. Johnson has a text now phone number and did not answer. This writer also texted her to request a call back.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Officer Johnson called this writer and informed that the residence is an apartment building and he did not know the apartment number. He said that the address that shows up in MVA is 2208 Eagle Street, Baltimore, MD 21213. This writer was able to find Ms. Johnson in CIS and found that the apartment number is A. This writer provided the information to Officer Johnson. Officer Johnson called back and informed that he was not able to access the apartment as he needed to be buzzed in and received no answer and no one else was able to let him in. This writer informed that I would continue to try to speak with the reporter to get more information and send Officers back out later if I am able to determine that Major is home.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">1:52 pm - this writer called Morgan Johnson to get more information. She did not answer and did not respond to requests to call this writer back. This writer requested a child welfare check from Baltimore County Police (CC #: 211351201). Officer Johnson was still working and called this writer back. He informed that he was able to get into the building earlier and it didn’t sound like anyone was home. He said that they already had it on their schedule for the next shift to go out to the home one more time. This writer informed that this would be fine and they could call AH with the outcome.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">3:23 pm - Officer Cain called this writer and informed that she went back out to the home and was&nbsp;not able to gain access to the building. She said that they would be willing to go back out and advised to call to request another check.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HISTORY</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Child Welfare:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No Child Welfare History</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">MJCS:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No Criminal History</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">SOR:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No registrants by name or address&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">This writer was unable to complete a background clearance on Larry since no last name or DOB was provided.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p>THIS REFERRAL WAS RECEIVED AFTER HOURS AND REVIEWED BY SUPERVISOR NEXT BUSINESS DAY FOR APPROVAL-LH 5/17/21</p><p>Police report in documents, no contact was made by LE</p><p>Unable to clear Larry due to lack of info </p><p>Referral submitted for CPS AR response</p>",
